  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Ganj Nameh, rock inscription</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Ganj Nameh (or Gandj Nameh) is a site located approximately 12 km southwest of Ecbatana. Two trilingual Achaemenid royal inscriptions are to be found here. One of these was ordered by Darius the Great (r. \u2009522\u2013486 BCE) and the other by his son, Xerxes the Great (r. \u2009486\u2013465 BCE).",
